<title>USA: Vastar Resources Inc Q1 shr rises.</title>
<headline>Vastar Resources Inc Q1 shr rises.</headline>
<dateline>HOUSTON 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>For the three months</p>
<p>							    ended March 31,</p>
<p>								1997     1996</p>
<p>REVENUES</p>
<p> Sales and other operating revenues	    $1,104.5  $758.7</p>
<p> Other revenues					     1.9     3.5</p>
<p> Gross revenues					 1,106.4   762.2</p>
<p> Less: Purchases					(799.1) (523.1)</p>
<p>	 Delivery expenses			     (23.7)  (12.3)</p>
<p> Net revenues					     283.6   226.8</p>
<p>EXPENSES</p>
<p> Operating expenses					32.7    32.5</p>
<p> Dry hole costs					    26.4     8.7</p>
<p> Other exploration expenses			    37.6    24.8</p>
<p> Undeveloped leasehold amortization		   6.8     6.3</p>
<p>Depreciation, depletion and</p>
<p>  amortization					     70.6    63.3</p>
<p>Selling, general and</p>
<p>  administrative expenses				14.7    12.2</p>
<p> Taxes other than income taxes			 14.6    10.0</p>
<p> Interest expense					  13.0    13.4</p>
<p> Total expenses					   216.4   171.2</p>
<p> Income before income taxes			    67.2    55.6</p>
<p> Income tax provision (benefit)			 4.3     0.0</p>
<p> Net income						  62.9    55.6</p>
<p> Earned per share*					 0.65    0.57</p>
<p>March 31, 1997 and 1996, were 97,260,759 and 97,250,001, respectively.</p>
<p>			    VASTAR RESOURCES, INC.</p>
<p>			    SUMMARY OF OPERATIONS</p>
<p>				  (Unaudited)</p>
<p>						     For the three months</p>
<p>							    ended March 31,</p>
<p>							    1997	 1996</p>
<p>OPERATIONS</p>
<p> Total production (MMcfed-net)		    1,181     1,160</p>
<p>Natural gas:</p>
<p>  Production (MMcfd-net)				874	 887</p>
<p>  Average wellhead price (per Mcf)		$2.31     $1.57</p>
<p>Crude oil:</p>
<p>  Production (Mbd-net)				 33.8	34.9</p>
<p>  Avg realized price (per barrel)		 24.14     19.36</p>
<p>Natural gas liquids:</p>
<p>  Production (Mbd-net)				 17.3	10.6</p>
<p>  Avg realized price (per barrel)		 15.51     14.25</p>
<p>Discretionary Cash</p>
<p>  Flow* ($millions)				   268.6     158.9</p>
<p>NATURAL GAS MARKETING</p>
<p> Sales (MMcfd-net)				    3,667     2,516</p>
<p> Average sales price (per Mcf)		     2.64	2.52</p>
<p> Margin** ($millions)				  10.6	27.1</p>
<p>	   (Millions of dollars except per share amounts)</p>
<p>*Discretionary cash flow is derived by adjusting net income for the</p>
<p>pre-tax effects of exploration expenses, depreciation, depletion and</p>
<p>amortization, and the change in deferred income taxes. Discretionary</p>
<p>cash flow is not a term defined by generally accepted accounting</p>
<p>principles and should not be considered as an alternative to net cash</p>
<p>provided by operating activities.</p>
<p>**Margin reflects the pretax income from gas marketing activities</p>
<p>before related staff and support costs. SOURCE  Vastar Resources, Inc.</p>
